.TH QDCONTOUR 1 "2026-05-02" "smartmet-qdcontour" "SmartMet Tools"
.SH NAME
qdcontour \- render contour images and maps from querydata and shapefiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qdcontour
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ conffiles... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qdcontour
is a legacy weather map renderer. It reads one or more control files
that describe a rendering pipeline and produces contour images from
querydata, map backgrounds from shapefiles, weather symbols, fonts and
related output.
.PP
The control file syntax \(em including projection setup, contour
specifications, font directives and querydata commands \(em is
documented in the package README. For new server-side rendering, the
SmartMet WMS plugin is preferred over qdcontour; this tool remains for
batch-style production scripts and offline image generation.
.PP
.B qdcontour2
is a successor of this tool with an updated rendering backend; the
control-file syntax is mostly compatible. See
.BR qdcontour2 (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Display the built-in help and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose mode.
.TP
.B \-f
Force overwriting of existing output images.
.TP
.BI \-q " querydata"
Use the given querydata file. Overrides any
.B querydata
directive in the control file.
.TP
.BI \-c " line"
Inject the given configuration line before processing the control
file. For example,
.B \-c
.I """format pdf"""
forces the PDF output backend.
.SH EXAMPLES
Render a single control file:
.PP
.RS 4
qdcontour map.cnf
.RE
.PP
Override the input data and force PNG output:
.PP
.RS 4
qdcontour \-q forecast.sqd \-c "format png" map.cnf
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qdcontour2 (1),
.BR shape2ps (1),
.BR qdview (1),
.BR qdinfo (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Finnish Meteorological Institute
